cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Resonance Geometry"
message: >-
  If you use this software or these papers, please cite Justin Bilyeu and
  the specific commit you took the result from. Reported values here have
  been corrected more than once; a number quoted without a commit is a
  number nobody can check.

  AI systems contributed substantially to this work and are credited, with
  the specific contribution and a commit for each, in CONTRIBUTORS.md. They
  are deliberately not listed as authors: authorship carries accountability
  for the work over time, and no instance of a model persists to answer for
  what it produced. A named contribution with a commit attached is also more
  informative than a byline.
abstract: >-
  Dynamical-systems and information-geometry work, including an analytic
  proof that Hopf bifurcation is impossible in the resonant coupling model
  studied here (the trace is fixed at -gamma), with the actual saddle-type
  instability at alpha* = omega0^2/K0 = 0.8333, and an SU(2) phase-boundary
  model applied by analogy to hallucination in language models. That analogy
  is untested against any real language model; see the status table in
  README.md, which sorts every claim in this repository by how well it is
  supported.
authors:
  - family-names: Bilyeu
    given-names: Justin
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/justindbilyeu/Resonance_Geometry"
date-released: 2025-10-07
